{"assets":["/statement-assets/f4651c93c4c3fc6439eba432d594b1a8c8f2e12dc19d67d6a5b63fa7a236d265.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1680","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Lenient Vertex Cover"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a simple connected undirected graph, consisting of $$$n$$$ vertices and $$$m$$$ edges. The vertices are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A vertex cover of a graph is a set of vertices such that each edge has at least one of its endpoints in the set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lenient"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertex cover such a vertex cover that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" edge in it has both endpoints in the set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lenient"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertex cover of a graph or report that there is none. If there are multiple answers, then print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 10^6$$$; $$$n - 1 \\le m \\le \\min(10^6, \\frac{n \\cdot (n - 1)}{2})$$$) — the number of vertices and the number of edges of the graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$m$$$ lines contains two integers $$$v$$$ and $$$u$$$ ($$$1 \\le v, u \\le n$$$; $$$v \\neq u$$$) — the descriptions of the edges."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, the graph is connected and doesn't have multiple edges. The sum of $$$n$$$ over all testcases doesn't exceed $$$10^6$$$. The sum of $$$m$$$ over all testcases doesn't exceed $$$10^6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, the first line should contain "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lenient"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertex cover exists, and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise. If it exists, the second line should contain a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, where $$$s_i = 1$$$ means that vertex $$$i$$$ is in the vertex cover, and $$$s_i = 0$$$ means that vertex $$$i$$$ isn't."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, then print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kin